  "body": "Stacked on #2662 (merge #2662 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nMove shows the three move arrows and the three rotate rings together.\nA ring drag turns the part about its centre and the chosen axis.\nThe existing command supplies one undo step and marks the toolpath stale.\n\nThe bar offers Move value and Rotate value editors.\nThese controls keep both handle sets visible.\nA drag selects its matching editor.\nThe legacy Rotate shortcut selects the angle editor while Move is active.\nThe angle snap step remains editable, with the existing 90 degree default.\n\nEdge-on rings show an orbit hint and refuse an inert drag.\nEach handle has a named AccessKit Button node.\nUnavailable rings have a disabled node.\nThe viewport layout test covers the extra editor row.\n\nBefore: Move shows arrows only.\n\n![Move gizmo before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d067bdfb572e463de92c71cd99f61e315accc40/2624/before.png)\n\nAfter: Move shows arrows and rings, with the angle editor selected.\n\n![Move gizmo after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d067bdfb572e463de92c71cd99f61e315accc40/2624/after.png)\n\nThe fork stores these images only on its pr-screenshots branch.\nThe issue branch contains the decision record in docs/decisions/2624-combined-gizmo.md.\nThe existing move_model MCP tool already supports a turn with a pivot.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Move and Rotate flags disabled each other.\nThe typed editor also used those flags to choose between distance and angle.\nAn edge-on ring accepted a press through a fallback angle and started an inert drag.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe first two pins failed on unchanged production code:\n\n- move_gizmo_shows_arrows_and_rings_together\n- an_edge_on_ring_refuses_the_drag_and_names_the_view_change\n\nThe combined Move route also passes these tests:\n\n- a_ring_drag_is_one_undoable_turn_that_stales_the_path_and_carries_the_stock\n- shift_drag_snaps_to_the_bar_angle_step\n- changing_snap_step_in_the_bar_changes_shift_drag_snap\n- typing_an_angle_in_the_bar_turns_the_part_about_the_chosen_axis_as_one_undo_step\n- combined_gizmo_exposes_each_handle_and_keeps_both_value_editors_reachable\n- edge_on_ring_accessibility_is_disabled_while_the_visible_ring_stays_enabled\n- layout_page_viewport\n\nSix mutation groups failed their pins and passed after restoration:\n\n- Restore the old Move flags.\n- Bypass the legacy Rotate preservation guard.\n- Restore the old edge-on press behavior.\n- Restore the old typed editor choice from #2662.\n- Restore the old ring painter without AccessKit nodes.\n- Keep the nodes but remove their disabled state.\n\nThe old guards came from upstream/main.\nThe mutation kept the parent PR APIs so the pins failed on assertions.\nThe old typed controls came from #2662 because upstream/main has no such module.\n\nFinal checks passed after all source changes:\n\n- cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main: 17 of 17 steps passed; 1355 tests passed, 9 ignored, 0 failed.\n- cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings: no warnings or errors.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The issue diff and the stacked PR diff change no NC or CL files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nRelease snapshots, heavy playback benchmarks, manual image suites, and an interactive desktop session.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2662 supplies the base. The overlaps include turn_drag::press, turn_handles::draw, and viewport_bar::controls::draw.\n- #2783 touches viewport_bar.rs and viewport_bar_tests.rs in different functions; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2773, #2770, #2764, and #2663 touch page_layout.rs in different functions; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The part movement gizmo now shows rotate rings with its move arrows, supports typed turns and snapping, and explains unavailable rings.\n\nFixes #2624\n",
